# External Plugins Bridge — runnable .http examples
#
# Prerequisites:
#   1. Control Plane API running locally (default: http://localhost:5149).
#   2. ExternalPlugins__Plugins__0__Name and ExternalPlugins__Plugins__0__BaseUrl
#      configured, for example through .env (committed placeholders) or .env.local
#      (gitignored). The example below assumes a plugin named "sample" that exposes
#      a remote operation "ping".
#
# Secrets: HOST and PROJECT_ID come from .env via {{$dotenv ...}}. Never commit a
# real hostname, address, or credential here; override locally in .env.local.

@HOST = {{$dotenv HOST}}
@PROJECT_ID = {{$dotenv PROJECT_ID}}

###
# Execute an external operation through the host. The bridge exposes the remote
# operation as {pluginName}.{remoteId}. RequiresConfirmation is metadata only; the
# host does not enforce it in this slice.

POST {{HOST}}/api/operations/execute
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "projectId": "{{PROJECT_ID}}",
  "operationId": "sample.ping",
  "requestedBy": "engineer@example.com",
  "input": {}
}

###
# Retrieve the last 20 operation executions (includes external plugin history).

GET {{HOST}}/api/operations/history?take=20
Accept: application/json
